// corpus: known-failure a lazy walk over more than a few thousand elements stays unevaluated (ROADMAP: "Default iteration limit of 1024 for Epsil programs")
// Project Euler 4: the largest palindrome that is a product of two 3-digit
// numbers. The comprehension has 5050 elements; `max` over it is held.
isPalindrome(n) = integerDigits(n) == reverse(integerDigits(n))
max(filter([a * b for a in 900..999, b in a..999], isPalindrome))
// ➔ 906609
